                <pb facs="0224" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg136"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goodnow to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Goodnow reports that the Russian cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Askold</hi>
                    arrived at Shanghai to-day in a badly damaged condition, and that the taotai
                    informed the Russian consul-general that the vessel can not remain at Shanghai
                    for more than twenty-four hours, to which the Russian consul-general objects,
                    claiming that the <hi rendition="#italic">Askold</hi> can remain there for
                    repairs, etc., for a reasonable time.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
